-- title:
--   Closed-immersion section of π on the fibre at q from a chart retraction
-- statement:
--   Fix $N_0$ with $N_0\neq 0$ and a prime $q$ with $q\nmid N_0$, and let $R_q$ be the base ring over which the two-chart Igusa models are built, so that $\mathrm{toBase}\,N_0\,q$ is the structure morphism $\mathrm{igusaTo}\,(N_0q)\,q$ and $\mathrm{toBase0}\,N_0\,q$ is $\mathrm{igusaTo}\,N_0\,q$. The data are: a morphism $\pi$ from the level-$N_0q$ model to the level-$N_0$ model commuting with these two structure morphisms; an $R_q$-algebra map $\iota_0$ from $\mathrm{chartAlgFin}\,N_0\,q$ (the elements of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldFull}\,N_0$ integral over the $R_q$-algebra generated by $j$) to $\mathrm{chartAlgFin}\,(N_0q)\,q$ which is compatible with the two embeddings into $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,\mathbb{Q}$, and such that $\pi$ restricted along the $j$-finite chart inclusions $\iota_{\mathrm{Fin}}$ is $\operatorname{Spec}\iota_0$; an algebraically closed field $\kappa$ of characteristic $q$ which is an $R_q$-algebra, with $\kappa\otimes_{R_q}\mathrm{chartAlgFin}\,N_0\,q$ nontrivial; morphisms $c_0$ and $c$ from the spectra of $\kappa\otimes_{R_q}\mathrm{chartAlgFin}\,N_0\,q$ and $\kappa\otimes_{R_q}\mathrm{chartAlgFin}\,(N_0q)\,q$ to the fibres $\mathrm{fibre0}$ and $\mathrm{fibre}$ (the pullbacks of the two structure morphisms along $\operatorname{Spec}$ of $R_q\to\kappa$), pinned by requiring that their first projections are $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the right inclusion followed by $\iota_{\mathrm{Fin}}$ and their second projections are $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the left inclusion; and a $\kappa$-algebra map $\sigma_0$ from $\kappa\otimes_{R_q}\mathrm{chartAlgFin}\,(N_0q)\,q$ to $\kappa\otimes_{R_q}\mathrm{chartAlgFin}\,N_0\,q$ retracting $\mathrm{id}_\kappa\otimes\iota_0$. The conclusion asserts the existence of a morphism $\mathrm{comp}_0:\mathrm{fibre0}\to\mathrm{fibre}$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\kappa$ (it commutes with the second projections) which is a closed immersion, satisfies $\mathrm{comp}_0$ followed by $\mathrm{fibreMap0}\,\pi$ equals the identity, satisfies $c_0$ followed by $\mathrm{comp}_0$ equals $\operatorname{Spec}\sigma_0$ followed by $c$, and has the property that any point $x$ whose image under $\mathrm{comp}_0$ lies in the range of $c$ on points already lies in the range of $c_0$ on points.
--
--   This produces one of the two copies of $X_0(N_0)$ inside the fibre at $q$ of the Deligne–Rapoport model of $X_0(N_0q)$, realised as the image of a closed-immersion section of the base-changed forgetful map, starting from a retraction of the chart map on the $j$-finite charts. It is used in the construction of the pair of components of the fibre over a residue field, via [`ModularCurve.DRLevel.exists_comp_pair_fibre_residueField`](thm.html#ModularCurve.DRLevel.exists_comp_pair_fibre_residueField).
